Original commit body from 9ff4f6ed010a7895f82e2f2816aa208d33c1d201:

SYNTHETIC_FRAMEWORK_ROLES decides which linker nodes the enclosure pass
connects to the real function they sit in. It was a hand-written list
that drifted from what the linkers write:
- the Electron and Phoenix IPC linkers write ipc_send / ipc_receive (an
  f-string); the list said ipc_publisher / ipc_subscriber;
- message_sender / message_handler, crypto_producer / crypto_consumer,
  grpc_client, graphql_client, ipc_caller (tauri) and ipc_bridge_caller
  (electron) are call-site stand-ins whose linkers emit edges OUT of the
  node and none into it, and the list missed them;
- http_client was listed but is minted kind=call_site, and the predicate
  admitted function/method only, so it never matched -- nor did the
  database, subprocess and solidity-ABI call sites folded to call_site;
- six listed values had no producer (websocket_emitter,
  websocket_listener, ipc_subscriber, db_query, subprocess_call,
  abi_call), and grpc_server is minted kind=class, which never matched.

Now: SYNTHETIC_FRAMEWORK_ROLES holds the 18 call-site roles; every
kind=call_site node is a stand-in; NOT_ENCLOSED_FRAMEWORK_ROLES names the
8 other roles linkers write, each with a reason (declarations:
graphql_resolver, grpc_service, grpc_servicer, objc_bridge,
openapi_operation; kind not a call site: grpc_server, selector_ref; not
reviewed: dispatcher). ipc.py / phoenix_ipc.py share an
IPC_FRAMEWORK_ROLES table instead of the f-string, so the values are
literal. test_synthetic_role_partition reads the linker sources and fails
when a role is written that neither set names, or a set names one nobody
writes, or a new non-literal write appears.

Measured, survey on dev vs this branch:
- session-desktop (Electron): enclosure edges 125 -> 381. Before, 0 of
  the 43 ipc_send/ipc_receive, 111 message_sender, 93 message_handler,
  7 crypto_* and 2 http_client stand-ins had an edge from any real
  symbol; after, all of them do. All 262 new edges run from a function
  whose span contains the stand-in's line (checked on every edge). Node
  count unchanged (17,806).
- livebook (Phoenix + bundled JS): enclosure edges 327 -> 477; 0 -> all of
  the 31 ipc_*, 107 message_*, 11 http_client and 1 grpc_client
  stand-ins. 38 new edges are in source files and all are
  span-contained. The other 112 start in static/assets/ bundles, which
  are tier-filtered: their functions leave the output and their edges
  are kept through external_symbol placeholders -- dev already carries
  5,876 such placeholders there, 240 of them on enclosure edges. This
  adds 16 placeholders (16,231 -> 16,247 nodes). That linker stand-ins
  survive the tier filter at all is pre-existing and not changed here.

Tests: the partition (from the linker sources), the predicate per kind
and role, and the production Electron and Phoenix linkers through the
production _connect_synthetic_to_enclosing: an ipcRenderer.send /
broadcast! inside a function gets the uses edge from it. Mutation-checked:
dropping ipc_send from the set or the call_site branch reds 6 tests.

